 Agriculture Construction & Mining AMR (Warehouse) COMPANY Partners CAREERS NEWSROOM News Press releases Blog Videos Newsletters Products Cognata Off-Road AVBox OneSim DriveMatrix DriveMatrix Highway Dataset Sensor Hub (ADPH) ADAS Safety Regulations Simulation Autonomous Drone Simulation Sensor Simulation Closed-Loop Simulations Large-Scale Scenario Generation Off-road AV simulation Academy Validation White-Paper HIL – Hardware in the Loop DIL – Driver in the Loop Datasets DriveMatrix Highway Dataset Traffic Light Datasets Traffic Signs Pedestrian Datasets Vehicle Datasets Datasets White-Paper Autonomous Drone Simulation Industries Defense Autonomous Vehicles Smart Cities Agriculture Construction & Mining AMR (Warehouse) COMPANY Partners CAREERS NEWSROOM News Press releases Blog Videos Newsletters Off-road AV simulation Cognata’s AV off-road simulation is designed to test, train and validate perception and control challenges for terrains that do not offer a clear road definition and for paths that offer challenging conditions such as boulders, side slopes, difficult tractions, and more. Request a DEMO Paths and Passages AV driving on off-road terrain is more challenging than it seems. The AV needs to consider narrow trails, tunnels & bridges in order to validate the dimensions & angels needed for passibility, as well as detection and reaction to unexpected ends of drivable paths. In addition, vehicle physics comes into play – the autonomous vehicle needs to calculate vehicle dynamics versus paths tilt angles while not having road marks on a flat road surface for detecting free space, using detected surrounding objects (or none) only. Cognata’s simulation platform enables the creation of many use cases that the autonomous vehicle might encounter and the validation (and analysis) of such cases. Sensors placement and blindspots Off-road sensor simulation is facing challenging suspension and manoeuvring, trying to overcome the simulated sensor’s movements as well as overcoming blind spots created by the need to have a sheltered sensor placement. Cognata’s simulation platform can create multiple use cases with limited visibility by other objects, dust trails, vegetation, and ground blindspots as well as darkness, lights & shadows for validating driving situations with limited visibility and ground blindspots, in addition to teaching the vehicle to compensate for sensor movements due to a bumpy road. Scenarios & assets catalog Focusing on off-road AV training requires a special focus on two additional aspects: off-road scenarios and off-road assets. For the scenarios catalog, we have created a variety of different scenes designed to train and validate off-road driving from identifying a drivable path to overcoming obstacles and difficult road conditions. We have also created a rich catalog with off-road special synthetic assets such as people, obstacles, and special off-road elements. Choose your use-case area × Request a DEMO [hubspot type=form portal=6291401 id=c70e905c-da84-4963-913b-b0f0605f2b52] CONTACT US Have any questions? Send us a message. First Name Last Name Work Email Company Newsletter I would like to receive the Cognata newsletter Policy By submitting this form, you agree your personal information will be handled in accordance with Cognata's privacy policy. The datasets are governed by the Dataset License Terms * Send TERMS OF USE PRIVACY POLICY MEDIA KIT STANDARD EULA TERMS DATASET LICENSE TERMS OF USE PRIVACY POLICY MEDIA KIT STANDARD EULA TERMS DATASET LICENSE Twitter Facebook-f Linkedin-in Youtube All rights reserved © 2025 Cognata This website uses cookies to improve your experience. We'll assume you're ok with this, but you can opt-out if you wish. Cookie settings ACCEPT Privacy & Cookies Policy Close Privacy Overview This website uses cookies to improve your experience while you navigate through the website. Out of these, the cookies that are categorized as necessary are stored on your browser as they are essen